---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | The Spotted Ape"
  description="How The Spotted Ape (Pty) Ltd handles personal information under South African POPIA and, where applicable, GDPR."
>
  <article class="editorial-container editorial-container--narrow py-12 sm:py-20">
    <header class="mb-12 border-b border-[var(--border-subtle)] pb-9 sm:mb-16 sm:pb-12">
      <p class="technical-label mb-5 text-[11px] tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-kharos)]">LEGAL / PRIVACY</p>
      <h1 class="mb-6 text-5xl leading-[0.98] sm:text-7xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="max-w-[58ch] text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        This policy explains how The Spotted Ape (Pty) Ltd handles personal information when you visit our website or contact our studio.
      </p>
      <p class="technical-label mt-6 text-[11px] tracking-widest text-[var(--text-muted)]">LAST UPDATED / 17 OCTOBER 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-muted)] sm:space-y-12 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-editorial mb-3 text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">1. Responsible party</h2>
        <p>
          The responsible party is The Spotted Ape (Pty) Ltd, registration number 2023/953163/07, based in Cape Town, South Africa. For privacy questions or requests, contact us at <a class="text-[var(--accent-kharos)] underline underline-offset-4" href="mailto:contact@spottedape.com">contact@spottedape.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 font-[var(--font-editorial)] text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">2. Information we handle</h2>
        <p>When you make an inquiry, we may process your name, role and organization, team size, selected engagement or maturity stage, and the context you choose to provide. If you contact us directly, we also process the information in your message and the contact details needed to reply.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Please do not include special-category or highly confidential information in a website inquiry. Website hosting and security services may also process technical information such as an IP address, browser details, and request logs.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 font-[var(--font-editorial)] text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">3. Why and on what basis</h2>
        <p>We use inquiry information to respond to you, assess a potential workshop or advisory engagement, provide requested services, maintain business records, and protect the website. Under POPIA, we aim to process information lawfully, fairly, transparently, for a specific purpose, and only to the extent necessary. Where GDPR applies, our lawful basis will generally be steps requested before entering a contract, performance of a contract, legitimate interests, consent, or a legal obligation, as appropriate to the situation.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 font-[var(--font-editorial)] text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">4. Service providers and international processing</h2>
        <p>We may share the minimum necessary information with providers that host the website, deliver an inquiry to us, or support a service you request. If a submission endpoint is configured for the inquiry form, the information you submit is sent to that provider; otherwise, the form prepares an email to our studio. The site also loads typography from Google Fonts, which may receive technical request information from your browser. Substack is a separate service when you follow a publication link.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Some providers may process information outside South Africa or your country. Where required, we use appropriate contractual, security, or other safeguards for cross-border transfers. We do not sell personal information.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 font-[var(--font-editorial)] text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">5. Retention and security</h2>
        <p>We retain inquiry correspondence only for as long as reasonably necessary to respond, manage a resulting relationship, meet legal and accounting duties, or resolve a dispute. We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards appropriate to the information, but no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 font-[var(--font-editorial)] text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">6. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>Subject to applicable law, you may request access to or correction of your personal information, ask for deletion or restriction, object to certain processing, withdraw consent where processing relies on consent, or request a portable copy. You may also complain to the relevant supervisory authority. In South Africa, this includes the Information Regulator; where GDPR applies, it includes your local data protection authority.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Contact <a class="text-[var(--accent-kharos)] underline underline-offset-4" href="mailto:contact@spottedape.com">contact@spottedape.com</a> to make a request. We may need to verify your identity and will respond within the time required by applicable law.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 font-[var(--font-editorial)] text-2xl text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-3xl">7. Cookies and changes</h2>
        <p>This website does not currently use advertising or analytics cookies. Essential technical storage or cookies may be used by hosting or security infrastructure. We will update this policy if our practices materially change. The current version is identified by the update date above.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
